WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
An equation says that two expressions are equal. Apply the same operation to both sides to preserve equality.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Subtract three from both sides. The equation becomes two x equals eight.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Divide both sides by two. This gives x equals four.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Two times four plus three equals eleven. The solution is correct. Try solving three x plus two equals fourteen.
